WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.800
He's the much-loved monarch who sets the chaotic&nbsp;
events of "House of the Dragon" in motion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.360
but why was the so-called "Good King" so&nbsp;
popular? Here's a quick lesson on the show.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.620
"Game of Thrones" ended its epic&nbsp;
run back in May of 2019, and now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:17.820
"House of the Dragon" is bringing fans back&nbsp;
to Westeros in droves — though this time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.240
they're watching a story set nearly two&nbsp;
centuries before the original series.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:27.060
Focusing on the powerful, dragon-riding Targaryen&nbsp;
family long before their descendant Daenerys ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:32.160
traveled on dragonback, "House of the Dragon"&nbsp;
kicks off even earlier than that, with a council&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.660
that chooses Viserys Targaryen as the new monarch&nbsp;
when there's not a clear line of succession.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.740
Chosen over his cousin Princess Rhaenys&nbsp;
as the next King of the Seven Kingdoms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.960
Viserys is, on the surface, a fair,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.680
just king with a good heart who's always&nbsp;
trying to do what's best for the realm.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:51.240
"As king, it is my obligation to avoid&nbsp;
war until such time it is unavoidable."

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:55.500
With that said, it seems like those around&nbsp;
him don't take him particularly seriously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:01.080
and everyone from Rhaenys to her husband Corlys&nbsp;
Velaryon to the now-former Hand of the King,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:05.100
Otto Hightower, frequently outsmart and&nbsp;
manipulate the king for their own purposes.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:09.840
So who chooses Viserys as the next ruler of the&nbsp;
realm? Well, that would be the Great Council&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:14.280
of King Jaehaerys Targaryen, briefly played by&nbsp;
Michael Carter in the series premiere of "House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:19.800
of the Dragon." Why does Jaeherys loom so large&nbsp;
over Viserys, and what exactly was his legacy?

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:24.420
Known by the nickname "Good King," Jaehaerys&nbsp;
I was one of the most popular kings in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:28.920
history of the Seven Kingdoms. Though his&nbsp;
fellow beloved king Aegon the Conqueror was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:33.480
known as a fierce warrior and was the first&nbsp;
King of the Seven Kingdoms, Jaehaerys held an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.900
important record as the longest-reigning&nbsp;
monarch in the history of the realm.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.260
According to George R.R. Martin's&nbsp;
source material "Fire and Blood,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:43.860
Jaehaerys ruled the Seven Kingdoms&nbsp;
for a whopping fifty five years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:47.220
and by all accounts, they were&nbsp;
pretty uniformly good ones as well.

00:01:48.043 --> 00:01:52.680
Jaehaerys' legacy is also pretty storied; he's&nbsp;
credited with keeping the realm peaceful and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:57.480
prosperous, and he also was able to forge truces&nbsp;
between warring houses to keep things level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:02.400
including one between House Bracken and House&nbsp;
Blackwood, two houses of the Riverlands.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:07.500
In his youth, Jaehaerys was also a formidable&nbsp;
fighter, facing off personally against Dornish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:12.240
forces during a skirmish known as the Third&nbsp;
Dornish War, and in the early days of his reign,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:16.500
he more or less created a system of laws that&nbsp;
would govern the realm for centuries to come.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:21.780
Finally, he was also famous as a dragon-rider; he&nbsp;
rode Vermithor, who was the third-largest dragon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:26.760
in Westerosi history behind Balerion — whose skull&nbsp;
resides in the crypts of King's Landing — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:30.720
Vhagar, whose whereabouts are unknown during&nbsp;
the events of "House of the Dragon" so far.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:35.760
Faced with a lack of direct heirs, Jaehaerys and&nbsp;
his Great Council eventually chooses his grandson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:41.460
Viserys over his granddaughter Rhaenys, but did&nbsp;
he make the right choice? As the series opens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:45.600
Viserys is awaiting the birth of his second&nbsp;
child, whom he hopes will be a son; though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.220
it is, the infant dies along with Viserys'&nbsp;
first wife Aemma, leaving him heartbroken.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:54.480
Though he then names his daughter and&nbsp;
only child Rhaenyra as his official heir,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.820
he goes on to marry again and produces a son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:01.200
Aegon whose mere existence kicks off the&nbsp;
central conflict of "House of the Dragon."

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.760
Viserys is, for the first five episodes,&nbsp;
in miserably poor health and seemingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.180
ineffective. He's unable to shut&nbsp;
down the armies of the Stepstones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:12.223
leaving his brother Daemon and&nbsp;
Corlys to clean up his mess.

00:03:12.391 --> 00:03:13.480
"Add it to the chair."

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:19.800
At the end of "We Light the Way," the&nbsp;
fifth episode, the king flat-out collapses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:24.960
and who knows what his health will be like moving&nbsp;
forward. Episode 6 promises a massive time jump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:28.200
and whatever happens next, it's&nbsp;
all thanks to the "Good King."

